Portions derived from Mongoose OS mos
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following files are derived from the Mongoose OS `mos` tool:

    https://github.com/mongoose-os/mos
    Copyright (c) 2014-2019 Cesanta Software Limited
    All rights reserved
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

All of them have been modified.

  target/dp/dp.go
      from cli/flash/common/cmsis-dap/dp/cmsis_dap_dp.go. Retains much of the
      original structure -- SetDbgPower, DbgReset, selectAP, the AP register
      accessors and the block chunking loops -- with error handling, logging
      and the probe abstraction changed. The SELECT shadow and Invalidate are
      new.

  target/mem/memap.go
      from cli/flash/common/cmsis-dap/memap/cmsis_dap_memap.go. Largely
      rewritten: the CSW/TAR shadow, byte-sized access, the word-only fallback
      and the tracing are new. Retains the register definitions, the
      initialisation check, the auto-increment handling and the exported API
      shape.

  probe.go
      from cli/flash/common/cmsis-dap/dap/cmsis_dap_client_interface.go. The
      Status predicate methods and the Request/Op types come from the
      original's TransferStatus and TransferRequest/TransferOp, and the Probe
      interface follows its DAPClient method set. The Pin, Sequence and Config
      types, the block and sequence calls and all documentation are new.

  cmsis/client/client.go
      structurally follows cli/flash/common/cmsis-dap/dap/cmsis_dap_client.go
      in its command helpers (newCmd/exec/execStatus, info/infoString) and its
      DAP_Info accessor set. The packet encoding itself is the CMSIS-DAP
      specification's; the bodies, the Transport seam and everything from
      SWDSequence down are new.

  target/rp2040/flasher.go
      no code from the original, but ReadTargetReg, ReadTargetMem,
      WriteTargetReg and WriteTargetMem are named after the interfaces in
      cli/flash/common/target.go, reaching this module through target/mem.

The rest of this module was written for it and has no counterpart upstream:
the bit-banging drivers, probe/bitbang, cmsis/server and its transports,
cmsis/wire (whose constants are the CMSIS-DAP specification's), target/rtt,
target/rp2040 beyond the names noted above, and internal/simtarget. The
ARMv6-M debug register addresses and bit definitions in target/rp2040 are
from ARM's architecture reference manual, not from the original.

